{title: Shout for Joy}
{subtitle: Psalm 100}
{key: G}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [G] | [G] | [C] |
| [G] | [G] | [G] | [D] |
| [D] | [Em] | [C] | [D] |
| [D] | [G] | [G] | [C] |
| [C] | [G] | [D] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Shout for joy to the LORD, all the [C]earth
Serve [G]the LORD with gladness [D]
Come be[Em]fore him with joyful [C]song
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Know that the LORD is [C]God
He [G]made us, and we are [D]his
[Em]We are his people
And [C]the sheep of his pasture
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Enter his gates with thanks[C]giving
[G]His courts with praise
Give [D]thanks to him, bless his [Em]name
Shout [C]for joy to the [G]LORD, all the [D]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
For the [G]LORD is [C]good
His [G]steadfast love endures for[D]ever
And his [Em]faithfulness [C]to all generations
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Enter his gates with thanks[C]giving
[G]His courts with praise
[D]Give thanks to him, bless his [Em]name
Shout [C]for joy to the [G]LORD, all the [D]earth
{end_of_chorus}

